      "label": "B",
      "summary": "'Contractless behaviour' means the same semantics as the existing DynamicContractlessObjectResolver / ContractlessStandardResolver. Readable public properties and fields would be serialized even when get-only. On deserialization, constructor parameters would be matched to members by name, and settable members would be assigned. The minimal edit to the change: in `CreateContractlessMembers`, also include public members that have only a public getter, with `IsWritable: false`. Select the best public constructor whose parameters match member names and types, and pass those parameters as `constructorParameters`. Only report MsgPack007 when neither a parameterless constructor nor a matching constructor exists.",
